    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Daulton Varsho** (69.94) and **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) lead our offensive charge, both positioned as elite starts against suspect pitching. **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a high-upside matchup against Bieber, where his power-speed profile is amplified by a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the heart of the order. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda**\u2014assuming his assumed leadoff/two-hole role holds\u2014is poised for a breakout day against Lorenzen. The park factors favoring hitters, combined with the SP skill of the opposition, provide the perfect environment for these two to anchor our scoring. **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) remains an essential component of our game plan, specifically because of the matchup against Quantrill and his high sprint speed; that elite SB potential against a pitcher with a slow delivery is a massive catalyst for his elevated efficiency score.\n\nWhile **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.82) offers a rock-solid floor, the most difficult decision on the bench centered on managing our positional caps versus the marginal scores of mid-tier starters like **Masyn Winn** (43.09). **Masyn Winn** just barely squeezed out a start despite the intimidating presence of Schlittler on the mound; his sub-50 score suggests he is on the precipice of being benched in future iterations if we need to conserve game caps for higher-leverage situations. Meanwhile, our core remains bolstered by **Bryce Harper** (63.39), who continues to deliver consistent value regardless of the matchup. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Lawrence Butler** all on off-days, our bench is thin, meaning we are heavily reliant on **Kyle Karros** (56.04) and **Tyler Freeman** (53.48) to hold their own against Seymour. We are monitoring **Jonathan Aranda** closely, as the \"Lineup Pending\" tag introduces risk; if he drops in the order, his utility value will be reassessed instantly to avoid inefficient game-cap 